    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d570">

                <pb facs="0513" n="507" sameAs="frus:frus1939v04/pg507"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">365D.1163/128</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Phillips</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 424</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-01-20">January 20, 1939</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Secretary of State refers to the Department’s telegram No. 119 of November
                    30, 1938,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d570-f1"/> regarding the alleged expropriation by
                    the Italian authorities of properties of the Seventh Day Adventist Mission in
                    Ethiopia, and requests the Ambassador to endeavor to ascertain and report what,
                    if any, action has been taken by the Italian authorities as a result of the
                    discussions reported in the Embassy’s telegram No. 356 of December 1,
                        1938.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d570-f2"/></p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
